FILED s543a (Opus, 2026-11-16), found while probing the warm-cache question (scratch/s543a/probes/g.pl in the s543a worktree).  Not a location issue; a SILENT WRONG, pre-existing.

`grep BLOCK %INC` (the special hash in list context as grep's list) returns the EMPTY list in PCL; `keys %INC` works, and a plain `%h` works.

PROBE:
    my %h = (am => 1, b => 2);
    print join(",", grep { /a/ } %h), "\n";
    require Carp;
    print join(",", grep { /Carp/ } %INC), "\n";
    print scalar(grep { /Carp/ } keys %INC), "\n";
  perl: am / Carp.pm,/home/.../lib/5.40.3/Carp.pm / 1
  PCL : am / (empty line) / 1

MEASURED (g2.pl): `my @x = %INC` and `map { $_ } %INC` flatten fine in PCL; `grep { /PATH/ } %ENV` is empty too (perl: the PATH pair).  So it is GREP over a runtime-backed special hash (%INC, %ENV), not the flatten in general: read p-grep's argument path for a hash operand (a plain `my %h` works).
